  "zoom": 1
}


:: Story Stylesheet [stylesheet]
tw-story { color: #3b2a1a; }


:: A quiet word {"position":"100,100","size":"100,100"}
The lord asks you to find out why the miller of {village} will not grind his grain.
Journal: Find out why the miller of {village} has shut his mill.
[[Go to the mill->At the mill]]


:: At the mill [be_at:village:4] {"position":"250,100","size":"100,100"}
The mill is shut. The miller will say only that a lord's men came by night.
(set: $miller_spoke to true)
{giver} knows: The player went to the mill of {village}.
[[Tell the lord->The lord hears]]
[[Ask {rival} about his men->The rival answers]]
[[Let it lie->Silence]]


:: The lord hears [talk_to:giver regard:6] {"position":"400,50","size":"100,100"}
The lord hears it and goes quiet.
(if: $miller_spoke)[He asks what else the miller said.](else:)[He wants to hear it from the miller himself.]
Memory: The player told me why the mill of {village} stopped.


:: The rival answers [talk_to:rival regard:-2] {"position":"400,200","size":"100,100"}
{rival} smiles and denies nothing.
Memory: The player asked me about the mill of {village}.


:: Silence [wait:7 regard:-3 sorrowful] {"position":"400,350","size":"100,100"}
Journal: You let the mill stay shut.
